    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11894": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Swimming",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Coach, Swimming Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Assistant Coach, Swimming Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Assistant Coach, Swimming Position Status Limited Part-Time Budget Summary Base Pay $6,500 seasonal stipend Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The responsibility of the limited part-time Assistant Coach for Swimming is to assist the head coach in all aspects of the administration of the swimming program. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration, and active support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and Lasallian higher education. COACHING / ATHLETE SUPPORT : -Practice and game coaching. -Academic Advising -Budget Tracking -Social Media Management -Team stats and improvement tracking percentage based -Assist with team orders for team attire/sizes, etc. -Create daily practice groups -Recruiting – based off stats and athletes that fit profiles we are looking for, using online recruiting database using power index/ratings -Meet set up and software, meet manager/team manager -Evaluation of fundraising opportunities As an individual employed in a coach capacity, you are subject to the regulations of the NCAA . If at any time it is determined that you are in violation of such regulations, then by the provision of the NCAA enforcement procedures, you may be subject to corrective disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Business Analytics/Marketing/Business Administration. Playing experience at the college level and the ability to communicate effectively within the educational philosophy of Lewis University required. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Limited part-time; average 19 or less hours per week Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01608 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
