      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Workforce Project Manager Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Workforce Project Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Workforce Project Manager Position Status Full-Time Budget Summary Base Pay $58,000 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Workforce Development Project Manager oversees multiple aspects of training project management, including student recruitment andretention, placement assessment, and logistics. This role will also provide ongoing oversight andreporting on training programs, field audits, quality management, and training deployment. Theindividual hired for this position will aid team members in grant writing, and grantmanagement/compliance. For more information on our benefits, please click the link Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration, and active support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Assists in business strategy through industry research and forecasting -Assists in developing relationships with employers -Assists in developing new and nurturing current relationships with business associations, chambers of commerce, and intermediary organizations -Maintains ongoing relationships with assigned clients -Maintains relationships with employer partners and intervenes to address job- or training related challenges experienced by participants, with limited assistance from Senior Project Managers. -Customizes sets up and administers placements tests and other tests as determined by employer, funder, and training needs and requirements. -Makes informed recommendations to the Director on the design of curricula based on client needs and requirements as well as feedback from participants and instructors. -Assists in the creation of instructional materials including assessments, PowerPoint presentations, workbooks, handouts, instructor’s guides, and others are required by client needs and requirements. -Deploys training programs at IWE training centers and client facilities and assists in auditing trainers as required by the Institute’s policies and procedures. -Sets up logistics with clients and trainers for the effective delivery of the assigned training programs. -Assists in limited aspects of writing and managing grants for the assigned training programs. -Works closely with the Support Services team to execute the quality verification procedure on all documents, training materials, and other training accessories needed to execute training programs. -In collaboration with the Senior Project Manager & Director assists in addressing training and client issues that emerge as training is delivered. -Works closely with the Support Services team in collecting all necessary documentation for courses deployed. -Collaborates with the Project Managers & Director in the creation of reports as required by funders. -Assists in the recruiting efforts of projects as needed -Performs other assigned duties. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Organizational Psychology, Training, and Development, or a related field. Minimum of 2 years of experience in project management or program coordination, or related work experience. Intermediate to advanced Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, Word, and Outlook skills. MS Project skills are a plus. Knowledge of and experience in workforce education.Ability to cultivate and maintain strong working relationships with colleagues, vendors,clients, and partners.Sensitivity to socially and ethnically diverse communities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, Spanish fluency a plus. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Full-time Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01768 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
