    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11165": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, DPT Program Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, DPT Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, DPT Program Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $933.00 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The DPT program at Lewis University seeks to create an available pool of Adjunct Faculty candidates to teach courses in our Department of Physical Therapy beginning in January 2025. Interested individuals are invited to complete a faculty profile, attach a curriculum vitae, and transcripts for consideration. Ideal applicants will have clinical expertise in any of the following areas: acute care, neurologic PT, ortho and sports PT, pediatric PT, geriatric PT, research, cardiovascular and pulmonary PT, Integumentary and Oncologic PT, and other specialties. Rank and salary will be determined based on qualifications and experience. Responsibilities · Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. · Foster an educational environment that is supportive of the Lasallian Mission. Demonstrates thorough knowledge and proficiency in the academic field. Utilizes effective strategies to foster student involvement and participation in learning. Adheres to program schedules and deadlines in managing course-related tasks. Prepares and presents educational material in a clear, comprehensive manner. Regularly evaluates student progress and provides constructive feedback. Encourages and guides student participation in various educational exercises. Acts as an intermediary between students and the university, ensuring a smooth academic journey. Collects and analyzes student performance data to enhance teaching methods and learning experiences. Fairly evaluates student assignments, exams, and projects. Maintains open lines of communication with the Program Director and Course Coordinators, especially regarding student issues. Ensures uniform content and evaluation standards across different sections of the same course. Conducts annual self-assessments of teaching performance and sets objectives for future growth. Regularly updates course material and aligns it with the institution’s course consistency policies. Proactively suggests improvements for future course iterations. Exemplifies professional conduct and fosters an environment of inter-professional dialogue. Works cooperatively with various departments to create a supportive academic environment. Upholds and respects the core values, policies, and procedures of the Program, College and University. Minimum Qualifications Must be licensed or eligible for licensure as a physical therapist in the State of Illinois. Applicant should be proficient with computer technology and possess strong organization skills. · Preferred Qualifications DPT degree ABPTS Certification Residencies and Fellowships Prior college/university teaching experience Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00390 Posting Date 02/01/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
