      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty,  Computer Science (Graduate) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty,  Computer Science (Graduate) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty,  Computer Science (Graduate) Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Instructor Budget Summary Base Pay Per Class Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct Faculty in Computer Science needed to teach courses in software engineering, networking, and cybersecurity. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Teach one or more classes in-person and online, including evenings -Availability to hold office hours and meet with other faculty members and department chairs or directors when necessary -Serve as a model of professionalism and act as a resource for students within the teaching-learning environment Minimum Qualifications Masters degree in Computer Science or related field.  At least 3 years of professional experience. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Computer Science or related field Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00276 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Cover Letter MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
