    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12821": {
      "title": "Adjunct Medical Office Assistant (MOA)",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Medical Office Assistant (MOA) Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Medical Office Assistant (MOA) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Medical Office Assistant (MOA) Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay NA Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct faculty member to teach one or more classes in a designated area. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University’s Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission as a Catholic and Lasallian institution of higher education. -Teach one or more classes in a designated area Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: · Current Certified Medical Administrative Assistant ( CMAA ), Certified Clinical Medical Assistant ( CCMA ), or equivalent healthcare credential. · Minimum (3) years of recent professional experience working in a medical office, healthcare administration, or medical assisting role. · Demonstrated experience using Electronic Health Record ( EHR ) systems and healthcare technology platforms. · Strong knowledge of: o HIPAA regulations and patient confidentiality o Medical terminology o Insurance verification and billing processes o Appointment scheduling and practice management o Patient communication and customer service o Healthcare office procedures and workflows · Minimum of three (3) years of full-time teaching experience in healthcare, allied health, or health science education OR demonstrated experience providing workforce development instruction in a healthcare or related setting. · Experience teaching adult learners, workforce development participants, or career training students preferred. · Ability to prepare lesson plans, deliver classroom instruction, evaluate student progress, and support students preparing for industry certification exams (such as the NHA CMAA exam). · Strong communication, organizational, interpersonal, and classroom management skills. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications: · Experience developing or delivering Medical Office Assistant, Medical Administrative Assistant, or healthcare career training programs. · Experience working with community-based, workforce development, or grant-funded training programs. · Familiarity with industry certifications, externship coordination, and healthcare employer expectations. · Experience building relationships with healthcare employers, coordinating externships, internships, clinical experiences, or work-based learning opportunities. Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00489 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
