      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Early Childhood Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Early Childhood Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Early Childhood Education Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $821.00 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct Instructor, College of Education and Social Sciences, Department of Education, needed to teach courses in the areas of Early Childhood Education. Day time availability and personal transportation is required. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. Responsible to model, teach and promote the unit standards for the Department of Education as a critical transformative educator, a multicultural educator and a social justice advocate. -To teach one or more classes in the Department of Education at any one of the Lewis university sites -Availability to hold office hours and meet with other faculty members and department chairs or directors when necessary Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree preferred, master’s degree considered. Illinois Professional Educator’s License – Early Childhood Grade Levels. Previous teaching experience in specific subject matter or credential in the area of subject matter applied for. Experienced in using technologies such as Learning Management Systems (Blackboard). Preferred Qualifications Bilingual (Spanish/English) preferred. Essential Duties Work hours Adjunct; varies Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00351 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you hold an active Illinois Professional Educators License with at least one endorsement in one of the following areas: Early Childhood, Special Education Letter of Approval, Learning Behavioral Specialist 1, English as a Second Language, Bilingual Education? (yes or no) yes no Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Cover Letter Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Other Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
