    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11178": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | STA Adjunct, Chemistry Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home STA Adjunct, Chemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title STA Adjunct, Chemistry Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $735 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct faculty member to teach one or more classes (lectures and/or labs) in the Department of Chemistry. St. Augustine College is an independent, bilingual institution of higher education emphasizing those of Hispanic descent. We strive to build a bridge to fill cultural, educational, and socio-economic gaps. We are a teaching college and a mission-driven institution that serves the working student at our main campus and one satellite campus in Chicago, offering a Latino Education Model to provide access to higher education for Spanish speakers. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Effective teaching, content expertise -Experience in teaching online and/or using course learning management programs. -Teach classes which are offered at weeknights, weekdays, and weekends. -Facilitate class instruction -Evaluate student performance -Develop and update course syllabus using online learning management programs. -Input midterm/final grades -Complete all required training such as institute days, sexual harassment, learning management systems, technology -Student advising and mentorship -Developing partnerships with organizations (depending on the courses taught) -Maintain required office hours and tutoring as necessary Minimum Qualifications -Master’s degree in chemistry, or a related field. -Two to three years of experience in teaching, using a learning management system. -Oral and written bilingual skills (Spanish, English) preferred. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00452 Posting Date 10/14/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary To apply, please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and statement of teaching philosophy. All materials should be submitted electronically via the application site. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
