    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12862": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant, Library",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant, Library Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Graduate Assistant, Library Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Graduate Assistant, Library Position Status Part-Time Budget Summary Base Pay $7000 Annually with 75% tuition waiver Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Graduate Assistant in the Library reports to the Director of the Library and is responsible for assisting with the Library’s digitization projects, providing routine research services, and assisting the Library Director with the operations of the Library. The Graduate Assistant (GA) must be available to work nights (until Midnight), weekends, Super Study, and currently living or have future plans to live on campus while pursuing degree. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration, and active support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and LaSallian higher education. -Assist with the Library’s digital projects, including scanning and data entry. -Collaborate with library staff to compile data used for library assessment. -Provide routine research services to assist library users with the proper use of online databases, print materials and other library resources. -Assist the Director with Library operations, which may include interlibrary loan and course reserves, etc. -Assist with technical services projects, including de-selection and collection maintenance. -During Super Study supervise, coordinate and monitor the activities/duties of student workers in absence of the Circulation Supervisors -Perform all duties associated with opening and closing the library - Assist with technical services projects, including de-selection and collection maintenance. -Other projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required. Must be enrolled in and maintain satisfactory progress in a graduate program at Lewis University. Must have a demonstrated ability to work both independently and as a member of a team. Must have excellent customer service and organizational skills, as well as excellent oral and written communication skills. Must have some proficiency with computer applications such as Microsoft Office. Some evening, weekend and overnight hours are required. Preferred Qualifications Some previous library experience and familiarity with online coursework and online tools (e. g., Blackboard). Currently living or have future plans to live on campus while pursuing degree Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; minimum of 20 hours per week; The Graduate Assistant (GA) must be available to work nights (until Midnight), weekends and Super Study. This is a twelve month position. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01780 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12363": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant, Sport Clubs, Club Hockey",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant, Sport Clubs, Club Hockey Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Graduate Assistant, Sport Clubs, Club Hockey Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Graduate Assistant, Sport Clubs, Club Hockey Position Status Staff Graduate Assistant Budget Summary Base Pay $7,000 annual stipend and 75% graduate tuition waiver Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Student Recreation, Fitness and Wellness Graduate Assistant will assist in the management and implementation of the Lewis University Club Sports program with an emphasis on Club Hockey (3 teams) Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and respectful support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and LaSallian higher education. -Provide practice and game supervision and presence at Sport Club home events. -Assist with marketing initiatives and growth strategies for Sport Clubs. -Assist with Sport Club team travel when needed (includes driving to away —games/tournaments) -Assist with leadership development of Sport Club officers. -Assist with the coordination of club sport training and risk management. -Assist with the collection and tracking of all team paperwork (rosters, waivers, travel etc) -Assist with the development of sport club promotional materials including brochures, postcards, flyers, and newsletter material updates. -Assist with organization, inventory and maintenance of all Club Sports equipment and supplies. -Assist with the coordination of facilities, athletic trainers, event staff, weekly practices and competitions for Club Sport teams. -Assist with the development of a leadership development in-service program for Club Leaders. -Participate in Student Services and other University meetings as deemed necessary. -Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Minimum of a bachelor’s degree, CPR and First Aid Certification. Must be enrolled and make satisfactory progress in a graduate program at Lewis University. Must have strong initiative, leadership skills, oral/written skills and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Hours will vary with practices and with travel – minimum of 20 hours per week Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01702 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11148": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Economics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Economics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Economics Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $821.00 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The College of Business and Graduate School of Management at Lewis University seeks to establish a pool of potential undergraduate adjunct instructors on an ongoing basis to serve as dynamic and student-centered educators in service of the Economics discipline; https://www.lewisu.edu/academics/cob/index.htm Focused on experiential learning, and active engagement, adjuncts chosen to teach at Lewis will create a charismatic and professional learning environment for students of diverse learning backgrounds. Adjunct faculty report to their respective department chair and/or the dean and performs instruction-related duties and responsibilities in a timely manner and in accordance with the mission, policies and procedures of the University. The relationship of the adjunct faculty member to the student is one of teacher and facilitator of learning. Inspired by the University’s Mission values of Wisdom, Knowledge, Justice, Fidelity and Association, the Lewis Community declares that we are a Sanctified Zone where people are committed to working to end racism, bias and prejudice by valuing diversity in a safe and nurturing environment. Lewis University, sponsored by the De La Salle Christian Brothers, serves a diverse community and is committed to promoting diversity and inclusion on our campus as an equal opportunity employer. We invite applications from individuals that embody a commitment to diversity. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status and other protected status as required by applicable law. We are fully dedicated to providing opportunities for development of the whole person. To demonstrate this commitment, Lewis University wishes to build a culturally diverse workforce which strongly encourages applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Teach their course(s) either at the Romeoville (Main), Oak Brook and/or Albuquerque campuses; -Availability to teach during the weekday or evening or online; -Prepare course materials, syllabus(ai) and update Blackboard course shells ( LMS platform); -Participate in required University and College activities, trainings and certifications; -Provide support and guidance to students. -Cooperate with department chairs or other program faculty to assure quality and consistency across the program Minimum Qualifications -A Master’s Degree in the chosen or related discipline is required; for Economics courses, a Master’s degree in Economics with business experience preferred. -Possesses excellent communication, problem-solving, and organizational skills. -All hired adjunct faculty must successfully complete the Lewis University Online Teaching Certification Program. -Candidates must demonstrate a willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Physical Demands: Repetitive movement of hands and fingers – typing and/or writing. Frequent standing, and/or sitting. Occasional walking, stooping, kneeling or crouching. Reach with hands and arms. Visually identify, observe and assess. Ability to communicate with supervisor/students/colleagues. Regular physical attendance required. The physical demands and work environment characteristics described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations (in accordance with ADA requirements) may be made, upon request, to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Preferred Qualifications -Candidates are preferred to have a minimum of ten years in mid to senior management positions, whereas their professional experiences demonstrate mastery of the subject matter discipline in the classroom. -Candidates are preferred to provide evidence of prior quality teaching and/or training experiences. -Experience with Blackboard and hybrid delivery, not required, but desirable. Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; adjunct positions at Lewis University are teaching positions and may instruct one or two courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of adjuncts. Adjunct Faculty provide a quality learning experience for students on a semester basis. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00258 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary To apply, submit the following: cover letter, CV with contact information for three references, official transcripts and relevant syllabi and teaching evaluations. Application materials will be accepted on a continuous basis Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Documents Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11442": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Special Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Special Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Special Education Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $821.00 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct Instructor, College of Education and Social Sciences, Department of Education, needed to teach courses in the area of Special Education as well as supervise candidates in field experiences and/or clinical practice. Personal transportation is required. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. Responsible to model, teach and promote the unit standards for the Department of Education as a critical transformative educator, a multicultural educator and a social justice advocate. -To teach one or more classes in the Department of Education at any one of the Lewis university sites and/or online -Availability to hold office hours and meet with other faculty members and department chairs or directors when necessary Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree preferred, master’s degree considered. Illinois Learning Behavior Specialist 1 Professional Educator’s License or Elementary or Secondary Professional Educator’s License with an LBS1 endorsement. Previous teaching experience with students in special education required. Experienced in using technologies such as Learning Management Systems (Blackboard) and online teaching. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Adjunct; varies Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00355 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * I hold an active Illinois Professional Educators License with at least one endorsement in one of the following areas: Early Childhood, Elementary, Middle Grade, Secondary, Learning Behavioral Specialist 1, English as a Second Language, Bilingual Education. Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Cover Letter Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Other Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
