    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/9330": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Organizational Leadership, Professional and Executive Coaching Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Organizational Leadership, Professional and Executive Coaching Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Organizational Leadership, Professional and Executive Coaching Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $2,865.00 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The College of Business and Graduate School of Management at Lewis University seek to hire adjunct faculty to teach in our ICF ACTP accredited Professional and Executive leadership program and MAOL within our Department of Organizational Leadership and Management. For more on our programs see: https://www.lewisu.edu/academics/mals/ Focused on experiential learning, and active engagement, adjuncts chosen to teach at Lewis will create a charismatic and professional learning environment for students of diverse learning backgrounds. Adjunct positions at Lewis University are teaching positions and may instruct 1 or 2 courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of adjuncts. Adjunct Faculty provides a quality learning experience for students on a semester basis. Adjunct faculty reports to their respective department chair and/or the dean and performs instruction-related duties and responsibilities in a timely manner and in accordance with the mission, policies and procedures of the University. The relationship of the adjunct faculty member to the student is one of teacher and facilitator of learning. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. Department Specific Essential Job Functions: -Teach their course(s) either at the Romeoville (Main), Oak Brook and/or Albuquerque campuses; -Availability to teach during the evening or online (synchronously online at a set time each week 6-9pm central time); -Prepare course materials, syllabus(ai) and update Blackboard course shells ( LMS platform); -Participate in required University and College activities, trainings and certifications; -Provide support and guidance to students. -Cooperate with department chairs or other program faculty to assure quality and consistency across the program Minimum Qualifications - Doctoral degree in a leadership related field (leadership, organization development, I/O psychology). - Current International Coach Federation certification ( PCC or MCC preferred). - Possesses excellent communication, problem solving, and organizational skills. - Candidates must demonstrate a willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. - Familiarity with the ICF competencies. - ICF assessment experience preferred but not required. - All hired adjunct faculty must successfully complete the Lewis University Online Teaching Certification Program. Preferred Qualifications -Candidates are preferred to provide evidence of prior quality teaching and/or training experiences. -Experience with Blackboard and hybrid delivery, not required, but desirable. Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00264 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a terminal degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Cover Letter Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12896": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Instructional Technologist Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Instructional Technologist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Instructional Technologist Position Status Full-Time Budget Summary Base Pay $58,355 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Reporting to the Director of the Faculty Center for the Advancement of Teaching and Learning, the Instructional Technologist is responsible for supporting faculty, staff, and students in the effective use of instructional technologies that enhance teaching, learning, and student success. Working collaboratively with the Faculty Center team, the Instructional Technologist provides technology consultation, training, troubleshooting, and instructional support for learning technologies including the Learning Management System ( LMS ), digital learning tools, multimedia resources, and emerging educational technologies. This position promotes excellence in teaching and learning by helping instructors integrate technology in ways that support learner engagement, accessibility, course quality, and the University’s Lasallian mission. The Instructional Technologist serves as both a technology specialist and a faculty partner, assisting with course development, faculty professional development, and technical support initiatives. Please click the link for more information on our benefits Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities Responsible to model the University’s Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s essential purposes as a Catholic and Lasallian institution of higher education. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Faculty Support and Consultation · Provide individualized consultations to faculty regarding the effective use of instructional technologies. · Assist instructors with integrating educational technology tools into face-to-face, hybrid, online, and HyFlex courses. · Recommend technology solutions that support pedagogical goals and student learning outcomes. · Collaborate with faculty on course enhancement and technology integration projects. Learning Management System Support · Provide support for Blackboard Ultra and related instructional technologies. · Assist faculty with course setup, content organization, assessments, gradebook management, communication tools, and analytics. -Troubleshoot LMS -related issues and coordinate resolutions with internal and external support teams. · Test new LMS features and communicate updates, enhancements, and best practices to faculty and staff. Training and Professional Development · Design and facilitate workshops, webinars, and training sessions on educational technologies and teaching best practices. · Develop training materials, tutorials, knowledge-base articles, guides, and documentation. · Support faculty development initiatives related to online teaching, course design, accessibility, artificial intelligence, and emerging technologies. · Promote the adoption of innovative teaching practices through technology-enhanced learning. Accessibility and Inclusive Learning · Promote accessible course design practices and Universal Design for Learning ( UDL ) principles. · Assist faculty in creating accessible course materials and multimedia content. · Support institutional efforts related to digital accessibility compliance and inclusive teaching practices. Help Desk and Technical Support · Respond to faculty support requests related to instructional technologies. · Diagnose and resolve technical issues or escalate concerns as appropriate. Course Development and Quality Improvement · Collaborate with instructional designers on course development and redesign projects. · Support Quality Matters and university course quality standards. · Assist faculty in implementing instructional technologies that improve learner engagement, retention, and success. · Provide recommendations for effective online and blended learning practices. Minimum Qualifications · Bachelor’s degree in Instructional Technology, Educational Technology, Instructional Design, Education, Information Technology, or a related field. · Minimum of two years of experience supporting instructional technologies in higher education, K-12 education, corporate training, or a related environment. · Experience supporting a Learning Management System (Blackboard, Canvas, Moodle, D2L, or equivalent). · Demonstrated knowledge of educational technology tools and instructional best practices. · Excellent customer service, communication, and interpersonal skills. · Strong organizational, problem-solving, and project management abilities. · Ability to work collaboratively with individuals from diverse academic disciplines and backgrounds. Preferred Qualifications · Master’s degree in Instructional Technology, Educational Technology, Instructional Design, Higher Education, or a related field. · Experience with Blackboard Ultra. · Experience providing faculty development and training. · Familiarity with accessibility standards, UDL principles, and Quality Matters. · Experience with multimedia production tools, video technologies, and AI-enhanced learning tools. · Knowledge of Microsoft 365, collaboration tools, and learning analytics. Essential Duties Work hours Full-time Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01783 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Portfolio Statement of Teaching Philosophy MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12488": {
      "title": "Academic Graduate Assistant, Biology",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Academic Graduate Assistant, Biology Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Academic Graduate Assistant, Biology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Academic Graduate Assistant, Biology Position Status Academic Graduate Assistant Budget Summary Base Pay Graduate tution Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Biology Department is seeking an outstanding candidate for a Graduate Assistant position for the 2026-2027 academic year. Ideal applicants should possess strong writing, analytical, and problem solving skills. Under supervision from the Laboratory Coordinator, the Graduate Assistant shall coordinate and perform a variety of duties to support laboratory courses and department projects. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration, and active support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Preparing materials for laboratory courses under the guidance of the Laboratory Coordinator -Assisting in special projects for the Biology Department Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a life science is required. Must be enrolled, and maintain satisfactory performance in a graduate program at Lewis University. Superior laboratory and communication skills. Proficiency with Microsoft Word, Excel, and Google Docs. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Part-time Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01008 Posting Date 05/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you enrolled in one of Lewis University's graduate programs? Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Other Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
