    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12900": {
      "title": "Director of Events and Conference Services",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Director of Events and Conference Services Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Director of Events and Conference Services Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Director of Events and Conference Services Position Status Full-Time Budget Summary Base Pay $82,407 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Under the direction of, and reporting to the Chief Operating Officer, the Director of Event Sales and Partnerships is responsible to develop and execute sales strategies to achieve revenue targets. The Director will drive revenue by prospecting and fostering relationships with both internal constituents and external clients. The Director is responsible to provide oversight to the Meetings, Events and Conferences ( MEC ) department through the development and execution of a comprehensive operational plan for both internal and external customers. Additionally, the Director is responsible for the overall vision, leadership and direction of the department, and MEC employees. Please click the link for more information on our benefits Office of Human Resources | Benefit . Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -The Executive Director is responsible for the overall vision, leadership and direction for the development and execution of all internal and external meetings, events and conferences. -Develops and manages a strategic plan for MEC including increasing revenue to the University through rentals and events. -Creates and manages processes, policies and procedures for the University’s Meetings, Events and Conferences including but not limited to contracts, fees, booking processes, and communications. -Using a mission-focused approach, oversee all events taking place through the MEC protocol and planning process. -Directly supervise and provide leadership to the Meetings, Events and Conferences staff. -Update and develop operational policies and procedures. -Respond to any immediate production requests or concerns, and successfully resolve client complaints or concerns. -Assess processes and data to evaluate events planned. -Make recommendations and assist in the implementation of changes for continuous improvement. -Foster purposeful positive relationships with campus partners, clients and vendors. -Develop internal and event survey systems as a means to achieve high customer satisfaction with internal and external events. -Demonstrate various supervisory methods and practices including: training, coaching, staff development and overall motivation of the full MEC department. -Exhibit exceptional event planning skills and experience to include: contract negotiations, space usage, catering, logistics, vendor relations, problem solving/trouble-shooting, strong communication and relationship building. -Spearhead strategic meetings with internal partners and all pertinent campus service providers, following up on issues/concerns, working to resolve problems and develop improved processes and procedures for future meetings, events and conferences. -Collaborate with the MEC staff to ensure the annual revenue goal of MEC is met or exceeded on an annual basis. -Work with Marketing to develop external marketing plan for facility usage to drive revenue to the University. Minimum Qualifications Prior related experience in events and conferences is required. Experience with contractual terms, restrictions and liabilities, is required. Ability to make administrative/procedural decisions and judgments. Strong interpersonal and communication skills required. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies. Knowledge and understanding of meeting and event planning principles, requirements, procedures, and available resources. Highly skilled in organizing resources and establishing priorities, facilities, technology and equipment. Ability to perform complex tasks and to prioritize multiple projects. Ability to use independent judgment and to manage and impart information to a range of clientele. Strong service orientation. Exceptional organization/time management skills. Good problem solving skills. Approachable and cooperative. Dependability and strong follow through on tasks. Ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Must be willing to work with flexible schedules involving evening, weekend and holiday hours. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Full-time; must be willing to work with flexible schedules involving evening, weekend and holiday hours. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01784 Posting Date 05/20/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Portfolio Transcripts MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11881": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Medical Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Medical Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Medical Assistant Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Instructor Budget Summary Base Pay NA Position Summary Information Job Description Summary This is an adjunct teaching position. Applicants must have knowledge of the role of the Medical Assistant, current Electronic Health Record practices and procedures, basic billing and coding practices and procedures that are commonly used in physician clinics, outpatient departments of hospitals and medical groups, and other healthcare facilities. The position may include day and/or night instruction . Rank and salary will be determined based on qualifications and experience. · Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Foster an educational environment that is supportive of the Lasallian Mission. -Maintain an approved syllabus and daily lesson plan outlining course content and learning objectives -Utilize a variety of teaching techniques to accommodate the learning styles of a diverse student body -Administer and grade quizzes, tests, and exams -Actively work to maintain a high level of student enrollment by maintain accurate daily attendance and communicating attendance and other student concerns with the Director of the Medical Assistant program -Assess student learning, skills, and competencies in electronic health records and in identifying and applying codes used in medical diagnoses and diagnostic procedures -Assess student progress in achieving the learning outcomes, program outcomes, and institutional outcomes appropriate to patient electronic health records, and medical billing and coding -Implement the learning objectives and program objectives as outlined in the course syllabus provided to them Minimum Qualifications • Have at least an AAS degree in any Health Administration Course or Computer Science from an accredited institution recognized by the U.S. Department of Education. • Have at least two years of teaching experience • Have at least four years of proven experience in the medical field, preferably in HIT Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree preferred. Teaching experience in Medical Billing and Coding and Electronic Health Records. Certification from American Academy of Professional Coders ( AAPC ) Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00476 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Transcripts Resume Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/10268": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, College of Business, Business Analytics Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, College of Business, Business Analytics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, College of Business, Business Analytics Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Instructor Budget Summary Base Pay Per class Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The College of Business and Graduate School of Management seeks to establish a pool of potential graduate adjunct instructors to serve as dynamic and student-centered educators in service of the following academic areas: Business Analytics, Business Statistics, Data Visualization, Data Warehousing. For more information on our programs visit: https://www.lewisu.edu/academics/cob/index.htm Focused on experiential learning, and active engagement, adjuncts chosen to teach at Lewis will create a charismatic and professional learning environment for students of diverse learning backgrounds. Adjunct positions at Lewis University are part-time teaching positions and may instruct 1 or 2 courses each semester on an “as needed” basis. This posting may or may not result in the hiring of adjuncts. Adjunct Faculty provide a quality learning experience for students on a semester basis. Adjunct faculty report to their respective department chair and/or the dean and perform instruction-related duties and responsibilities in a timely manner and in accordance with the mission, policies and procedures of the University. The relationship of the adjunct faculty member to the student is one of teacher and facilitator of learning. Inspired by the University’s Mission values of Wisdom, Knowledge, Justice, Fidelity and Association, the Lewis Community declares that we are a Sanctified Zone where people are committed to working to end racism, bias and prejudice by valuing diversity in a safe and nurturing environment. Lewis University, sponsored by the De La Salle Christian Brothers, serves a diverse community and is committed to promoting diversity and inclusion on our campus as an equal opportunity employer. We invite applications from individuals that embody a commitment to diversity. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status and other protected status as required by applicable law. We are fully dedicated to providing opportunities for development of the whole person. To demonstrate this commitment, Lewis University wishes to build a culturally diverse workforce which strongly encourages applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Teach one or more classes per semester on an as needed basis, either at the Romeoville and/or Oakbrook campus. -Availability to teach course(s) at the Romeoville and/or Oakbrook campus -Availability to teach during the weekday, evening and online -Prepare course materials, syllabus(ai) and update Blackboard course shells ( LMS platform) -Participate in required University and College activities, trainings and certifications -Provide support and guidance to students -Cooperate with department chairs or other program faculty to assure quality and consistency across the program Minimum Qualifications A Master’s degree in the chosen or related discipline is required. For example, for Business Analytics courses a Master’s degree in Business Analytics, Management Sciences, or Management Information Systems is the minimum requirement. Three years of professional or industry experience in the specific subfield being taught. Candidates who have evidence of prior quality teaching and/or training experience required and who indicate a willingness to be flexible in class scheduling. Possess excellent communication, problem-solving, and organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications PhD in the chosen or related discipline (Business Analytics, Management Science or Management Information Systems) is preferred. Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00255 Posting Date 02/16/2022 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary To apply. submit the following: cover letter, CV with contact information for three references, official transcripts and relevant syllabi and teaching evaluations. Application materials will be accepted on a continuous basis. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Other Documents Portfolio MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12687": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant, Continuing Education",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant, Continuing Education Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Graduate Assistant, Continuing Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Graduate Assistant, Continuing Education Position Status Staff Graduate Assistant Budget Summary Base Pay $7,000 annual stipend and 75% graduate tuition waiver Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Continuing Education Graduate Assistant will support strategic initiatives that expand Lewis University’s continuing education, workforce development, micro-credential, and lifelong learning ecosystem. This role combines marketing, operational support, learner engagement, digital innovation, and AI-enabled workflow support to help scale the impact and visibility of continuing education programs. This position is ideal for a graduate student interested in higher education innovation, workforce development, digital learning, marketing, AI-enabled productivity, or operational strategy. The Graduate Assistant will collaborate with faculty, staff, and external partners to support initiatives that strengthen enrollment growth, learner experience, community engagement, and operational efficiency. The role also includes exposure to emerging AI tools, automation platforms, and agentic workflows that support modern continuing education operations, communications, and content management. Responsibilities Continuing Education Operations & Program Support - Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Support administrative and operational processes related to continuing education and workforce development programs. -Assist with enrollment tracking, learner communication, reporting, and program coordination across multiple continuing education platforms. -Maintain organized records, project trackers, SOPs, and shared documentation. -Support coordination of workshops, professional development programs, webinars, micro-credential initiatives, and community learning events. -Assist with data collection and reporting related to program participation, learner engagement, and operational effectiveness. Marketing, Communications & Digital Engagement -Assist in developing and executing marketing and outreach campaigns for continuing education programs and workforce initiatives. -Create and manage content for email campaigns, newsletters, social media, digital promotions, and learner communications. -Support website updates and content management for continuing education and micro-credential offerings. -Design promotional materials and digital assets using platforms such as Canva or Adobe Creative Suite. -Help strengthen visibility and engagement for continuing education initiatives across internal and external audiences. AI, Automation & Digital Innovation Support -Support the exploration and implementation of AI-enabled workflows that improve operational efficiency, communication, and learner support. -Assist with the use of AI tools for content drafting, marketing support, research synthesis, meeting summaries, workflow optimization, and administrative efficiency. -Support experimentation with automation and agentic workflows using tools such as ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Claude, Make.com, Zapier, or related platforms. -Help document and improve repeatable workflows, processes, and operational systems. -Contribute ideas and recommendations for leveraging emerging technologies to strengthen continuing education operations and learner engagement. Community & Learner Engagement -Support outreach and relationship-building efforts with students, alumni, workforce partners, and community organizations. -Assist in gathering learner testimonials, success stories, and program impact examples. -Help coordinate networking and engagement opportunities connected to continuing education and workforce initiatives. -Support initiatives that strengthen learner experience, accessibility, and adult learner engagement. Minimum Qualifications -Must be a currently enrolled graduate student at Lewis University. -Strong written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. -Interest in continuing education, workforce development, adult learning, digital learning, or higher education innovation. -Demonstrated curiosity and willingness to learn emerging AI tools and digital productivity platforms. -Familiarity with Microsoft Office Suite and Google Workspace. -Experience with social media, content creation, project coordination, or marketing support preferred. -Familiarity with AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Microsoft Copilot, Claude) or workflow automation platforms is preferred but not required. -Ability to manage multiple projects, work independently, and contribute proactively in a collaborative environment. -Strong attention to detail, adaptability, and problem-solving skills. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Minimum of 20 hours per week, flexible hours; year round position Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01756 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11155": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science, College of Nursing &amp; Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science, College of Nursing & Health Sciences Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Exercise Science, College of Nursing & Health Sciences Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Instructor Budget Summary Base Pay $933.00 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The Exercise Science program in the College of Nursing & Health Sciences invites applications for adjunct instructors. Instructors with the following areas of expertise are encouraged to apply: Fitness Assessment and Exercise Science Administration. Other areas of expertise within the discipline may be considered. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration, and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Develop and teach courses and labs in the Exercise Science curriculum -Availability to hold office hours and meet with program faculty when necessary -Serve as a model of professionalism and act as a resource for students within the teaching-learning environment -Instructors of online courses are required to complete training in online course delivery provided through the University. Minimum Qualifications Earned masters degree in Exercise Science or a related field. Evidence of at least 3 years of experience in the field, including expertise in the area to be instructed. Must hold certification through ACSM or NSCA . Preferred Qualifications Undergraduate teaching experience preferred. Essential Duties Work hours Varies; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00307 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Cover Letter MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
