    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12817": {
      "title": "Temporary HR Department Assistant",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Temporary HR Department Assistant Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Temporary HR Department Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Temporary HR Department Assistant Position Status Temporary Budget Summary Base Pay $21.00 per hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The HR Department Assistant is responsible for providing overall HR departmental support. Temporary positions are not eligible for benefits. This position is estimated to last approximately 6 months. Responsibilities Mission Responsible to model the University’s Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission as a Catholic and Lasallian institution of higher education. Commitment to a diverse culture and appreciation for all people. Communications -Meet and greet all customers to the HR office and ensure timely response of inquiries -Provide exceptional level of customer service to both internal/external customers -Distribute and send mailings - Create employee files and maintain a complex filing system for confidential employee files and records -When needed, assist HR Generalist in forwarding e-mails to appropriate HR representative for response -Answer HR phone calls and route to the appropriate person or department Data/Performance Management -On occasion, assist in verifying, entering, and maintaining employee data in the computerized database. -Audit all terminated files, I9’s, and background check forms per Retention Record Policy. -Maintain changes to the on-line directory and outlook address book for department, name, title, or other significant changes. -Scan and upload transcripts and other needed documentation to Banner. Onboarding Activities -Send State of IL W4s for processing new employees as required by the State. Other -Book and schedule rooms for meetings and trainings. Order food and equipment for meetings as needed. -Maintain / report office supply inventory needs to Sr. HR Generalist, Contract Specialist -Other clerical duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related field OR administrative experience supporting a human resources department. Must have the ability work independently in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to team-based management required. Must be highly confidential and be able to maintain sensitive information. Commitment to Catholic higher education and a diverse and inclusive environment is required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office systems required. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Monday-Friday 37.5 hours per week Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01773 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
