    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/8566": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Health Information Management Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Health Information Management Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Health Information Management Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Instructor Budget Summary Base Pay Per class Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct faculty to teach on campus in the College of Nursing and Health Sciences ( CONHS );  Adjunct faculty are responsible for teaching students in the Health Information Management program. Under the general supervision of the Director, the adjunct faculty are hired on an as needed basis. Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Serve as a model of professionalism and act as a resource for students within the teaching-learning environment -Maintain required certifications/licensure and demonstrate continuing competence in area of expertise -Participate in all course orientations with Lead Faculty as well as orientations related to Blackboard, technology, and information resources needed to fulfill teaching responsibilities prior to the start of the class -Initiate and maintain ongoing communication with Lead Faculty, and/or Assistant Dean throughout the course to discuss relevant issues and concerns -Discuss individual student problems with appropriate Lead Faculty, and/or Assistant Dean in a timely fashion. Provide anecdotal documentation as needed. -Comply with all requirements of the CONHS for teaching, i.e. annual OSHA , hepatitis/TB updates, CPR certification, license renewal, current CV, etc. prior to the start of the course as applicable for teaching assignment -Comply with all CONHS requirements for teaching, including orientation to the course and clinical agency as required, use of technology, providing students with contact information, responding to students within a reasonable time, following the CONHS grading scale, and posting grades in a timely manner -Be responsible for meeting site expectations for classroom/technology use and teaching at the site -Within two weeks of completion of the course, return all course materials (i.e. textbooks) and equipment to the Lead Faculty Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree. Must have schedule flexibility to be available for students, and to teach on the Romeoville campus. Excellent communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Phd, EdD or equivalent.  ( RHIA ) Essential Duties Work hours Vary; Teach on an as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00290 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Cover Letter Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Other Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/12860": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant, Womens Basketball",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Graduate Assistant, Womens Basketball Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Graduate Assistant, Womens Basketball Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Graduate Assistant, Womens Basketball Position Status Staff Graduate Assistant Budget Summary Base Pay $6,500 annual stipend and 100% graduate tuition waiver Position Summary Information Job Description Summary The responsibility of the Graduate Assistant for Women’s Basketball is to assist the head coach in all aspects of the administration of the women’s basketball program. Responsibilities Responsible to model the university Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration, and active support of the University’s Mission in Catholic and Lasallian higher education. -Practice and game coaching -Recruiting and scouting - Public Relations -Fundraising -Academic Advising As an individual employed in a coach capacity, you are subject to the regulations of the NCAA , the Great Lakes Valley Conference ( GLVC ), and Lewis University. If at any time it is determined that you are in violation of such regulations, then by the provisions of the NCAA , GLVC or Lewis enforcement procedures, you may be subject to corrective disciplinary action, up to and including termination of employment. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Must be enrolled and maintain satisfactory progress in a graduate degree program at Lewis University. Playing experience at the college level and the ability to communicate effectively within the educational philosophy of Lewis University required. Preferred Qualifications Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; minimum of 20 hours per week; year round position Posting Detail Information Posting Number S01751 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents Portfolio Other Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
