    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/11707": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Pharmacy Technician Program",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty, Pharmacy Technician Program Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty, Pharmacy Technician Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty, Pharmacy Technician Program Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay $933.00 per credit hour Position Summary Information Job Description Summary This is an adjunct teaching position. Applicants must have knowledge of sterile products, pharmacy compounding, institutional pharmacy, pharmacy law and ethics, pharmacy records and inventory management, and an extensive knowledge of pharmaceutical calculations. The position may include day and/or night instruction. Rank and salary will be determined based on qualifications and experience. Interested individuals are invited to complete a faculty profile, attach a curriculum vitae, and transcripts for consideration. Responsibilities · Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. · Foster an educational environment that is supportive of the Lasallian Mission -Maintain an approved syllabus and daily lesson plan outlining course content and learning objectives -Utilize a variety of teaching techniques to accommodate the learning styles of a diverse student body -Administer and grade quizzes, tests, and exams -Actively work to maintain a high level of student enrollment by maintain accurate daily attendance and communicating attendance and other student concerns with the Director of Pharmacy Technician program Minimum Qualifications A minimum of an associate degree from an accredited institution recognized by the U.S. Department of Education. A minimum of five years proven experience as a Pharmacy Technician. Possess industry certification. Previous teaching or training experience desired Applicant should be proficient with computer technology and possess strong organization skills. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Prior college/university teaching experience Essential Duties Work hours Part-time; as needed basis Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00471 Posting Date 02/01/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts Optional Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.lewisu.edu/postings/9148": {
      "title": "PAF/Position Details",
      "description": "Lewis University Employment Opportunities | Adjunct Faculty-Education, Literacy &amp; ENL/Bilingual &amp; Educ Tech Skip to Main Content Employment Opportunities Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Lewis University Mission Statement Directions Faculty Benefits Staff Benefits Human Resources Home Adjunct Faculty-Education, Literacy & ENL/Bilingual & Educ Tech Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job PAF/Position Details Position Details Position Title Adjunct Faculty-Education, Literacy & ENL/Bilingual & Educ Tech Position Status Adjunct Tenure Non-Tenured Rank Lecturer Budget Summary Base Pay NA Position Summary Information Job Description Summary Adjunct Faculty needed in one or more of the following education specialties: Reading Specialist, Bilingual/ ESL / ENL Education, Instructional Technology Responsibilities Responsible to model the University Mission through dedicated job performance, service excellence to constituencies, respectful collaboration and active support of the University’s Mission and Catholic and Lasallian higher education. Responsible to model, teach and promote the unit standards for the Department of Education as a critical transformative educator, a multicultural educator and a social justice advocate. —To teach in person or online one or more classes in Reading/Literacy Education, Emergent Bilingual Education, or Educational Technology —Availability to hold office hours and meet with other faculty members and department chairs or directors when necessary Minimum Qualifications Previous teaching experience with P-12 and adult learners in the subject matter applied for. Credential/coursework/degree in the area of subject matter applied for (Reading/Literacy, English as a New Language/Bilingual Education, or Educational Technology). Terminal degree preferred, master’s degree considered with extensive experience. Illinois Professional Educators License ( PEL ) with appropriate endorsements preferred. Experience in P-12 educational settings and with instructional technologies preferred. Experienced in using technologies such as Learning Management Systems (Blackboard) and online/high flex teaching, as well as data management. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Current and active knowledge in appropriate content areas; working knowledge of the requirements for endorsement and credentialing in the area applied for; demonstrated experience with and commitment to working with culturally and linguistically diverse student populations; able to support/mentor pre-service and in-service teachers and other education professionals. Experience appropriate to the position applied for: ESL / ENL /Bilingual — experience working with emergent bilinguals and TESOL standards, with proficiency in a language in addition to English preferred. Reading/Literacy — reading specialist experience and familiarity with ILA standards. Technology — experience with technology education and familiarity with ISTE standards. Essential Duties Work hours Adjunct; varies Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00374 Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions Summary Please also submit a copy of your transcript for your highest degree earned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Transcripts Optional Documents Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Other Documents MAIN CAMPUS One University Parkway Romeoville, IL 60446-2200 (815) 838-0500 (800) 897-9000 Lewis University is authorized to operate as a postsecondary educational institution by the Illinois Board of Higher Education . © 2025 Lewis University. All rights reserved. Email Webmaster ¿ Habla Español ? Site Index To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
